Vast Price Manager (VPM) — Terms of Use
========================================

This is a plain-language summary of the terms that apply to the published
VPM container image. VPM is closed source: this repository documents how
to run VPM, but does not contain and does not grant any rights to VPM's
source code.

1. Free to use. CryptoLabs grants you a free, non-exclusive license to
   pull and run the published VPM container image, for any purpose,
   including commercial use of your own Vast.ai fleet.

2. No redistribution of modified images. You may run the published image
   as-is. You may not modify the image (or its contents) and redistribute
   or republish it, under this name or any other, to any other party.

3. Third-party components. The published image contains third-party
   open-source software. Each of those components remains under its own
   original license, which continues to apply to it regardless of this
   license. Nothing here changes or overrides those licenses. This
   includes packages you choose to download yourself after the fact — for
   example, installing the optional Vast CLI to run machine self-test
   pulls in third-party packages (including one under the AGPL) directly
   from PyPI; those are not part of the published image, and each keeps
   its own original license once installed. See docs/self-test.md in
   this repository.

4. Provided as is. VPM is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
   express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of
   merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement.

5. No liability. To the maximum extent permitted by law, CryptoLabs is
   not liable for any damages or losses — including lost earnings, lost
   listings, or account issues on any third-party platform — arising from
   your use of VPM. You are responsible for reviewing what VPM does
   before you turn on any write capability against your own account.
